{"c":[{"id":"7b6c418ead30eff1","sum":"Undo is whole-field; Asks ask ask.scope first (stand-ins need answeringScope); <=8 unclear use sure. formInputs adds web comboboxes; a secret opener takes the next line. realfill-asks defaults to page. SC1 requests carry a Disclosure; tests use test/minted.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1642b5380f13f0bc","sum":"Undo: whole-field only. Ask: Jev ask.scope per field; stand-ins need answeringScope. Settled fields fill; <=8 unclear use sure, else unsure; no ambiguity/length refusal. AX closed selects show selection only; realfill keeps options, no legends/headings except radio groups.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"177848396eca6f4e","sum":"Helper undo covers whole-field replacements, not host/extension caret/selection/append insertions. Every Ask first asks Jev ask.scope per field; test stand-ins need answeringScope from helper/test/builders.ts or Asks refuse/ask back.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T132116Z-e94ee4791db7e513","text":"The helper executor replaces whole fields; caret/selection/append insertion runs in the host or extension and never enters the executor undo ledger.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T144012Z-e2952279328219e3","text":"Every Ask route asks Jev's per-field scope question (purpose ask.scope) first, so a test Jev stand-in must answer it: wrap it with answeringScope in helper/test/builders.ts, or Asks refuse or ask back.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0ec40e0d5ae540d2","sum":"Ask fills settled fields; <=8 unclear fields use sure, else unsure; no refusal for ambiguity/length. Chrome AX closed selects expose only the selection. realfill page walks keep options but no legends/headings except radio groups.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T144012Z-ef6cc9d6c94c61fb","text":"I3 ruling: an Ask never refuses for unclear fields or a too-long question; Jev's settled fields fill, unclear ones are asked beside them (AskIntent.sure) only when <= 8, else listed as left to the user (AskIntent.unsure).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T162248Z-4dec6eda4a1a65ff","text":"Chrome AX shows a closed select's selected option only, so realfill-asks' default reader desk has no menu options; --form-window page uses the page walks (helper/fixtures/recorded/realfill-pages), which keep no fieldset legend or heading except a radio group's.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b616cda88a55aeb3","sum":"formInputs synthesizes editable web comboboxes; a secret opener takes the whole next line; clauses respect quotes, literals from retained spans. realfill-asks defaults to page (reader for pre-V4). SC1 requests carry a Disclosure; tests wrap in test/minted.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f2b260f724b03eed","sum":"Form reading and redaction: formInputs synthesizes editable web comboboxes (formControls alone is incomplete); a secret opener takes the whole next line; instruction clauses respect quotes and model literals come from separate retained spans.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T164500Z-f23002306114cfa8","text":"Editable web comboboxes are synthesized by formInputs; formControls alone is not a complete inventory for retaining fill inputs.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T173911Z-5d012ef86eac725c","text":"A secret opener consumes the whole next physical line, including conjunctions in its value. Instruction clauses must respect quotes, and model literals must come from separate retained spans.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"18b4fb1a390dd6dc","sum":"realfill-asks defaults to --form-window page since I4 (reader for pre-V4 compares; slow-eval pins reader). SC1: every Jev/writer request carries a Disclosure the clients verify; test requests wrap in test/minted.ts; structuredClone drops it (clone the body).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T183953Z-6f2314940641602e","text":"realfill-asks defaults to --form-window page since I4 (the helper plans browser Asks on the page walk); pass --form-window reader to compare with pre-V4 runs. slow-eval's Ask sets pin reader for their P1 references.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T194509Z-1033502c97d598d1","text":"SC1: every Jev/writer request carries a Disclosure (privacy/disclosure.ts) that the clients verify; hand-built test requests wrap in test/minted.ts, and structuredClone of a request loses its Disclosure (clone the body, keep the object).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7bd01f8a829ee9fd","sum":"Privacy: request text is ModelText only, every slot needs a shapes.ts row, excluded values read [withheld]; Disclosure keys match KEY (note_1). Every app build runs privacy_gate.sh (acceptances, no Vercel opt-in, bundled PrivacyPromise.txt); release sets CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bf2aa89d755a6e5f","sum":"SC1: request text is ModelText only (derived for reformats; casts outside src/privacy/ fail sc1-boundary); exclude.ts counts lower/upper/digit; excluded values read in as [withheld]. Every slot needs a shapes.ts row. Field-format mints trace to their window source.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2925274083aef64a","sum":"SC1: exclude.ts high-entropy counts lower/upper/digit only (symbols broke B25 held-16); excluded values read in as [withheld]. Request text is ModelText only (own/t/descriptor/candidate/memoryText, derived for reformats); casts outside src/privacy/ fail sc1-boundary.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T200650Z-ffcd5d83b2f9fc55","text":"SC1 exclude.ts: the high-entropy rule counts only lower/upper/digit classes; counting symbols flagged corpus URL paths (51310/forms/greenhouse-apply) and broke B25 held-16. Excluded values become [withheld] at read-in; writes and memory refuse any text holding it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T211138Z-929a7c53a65ffe04","text":"SC1: request text compiles only as ModelText (privacy/disclosure.ts own/t/descriptor/candidate/memoryText); mint a reformatted value with derived(base, text), which refuses words the screen never showed. A ModelText cast outside src/privacy/ fails test/sc1-boundary.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6af8d35d2cbd1bc9","sum":"Field-format candidates carry fieldFormat provenance and assumptions through both verifier wordings; validation traces the mint to its window source. Every request slot needs a privacy/shapes.ts row, or verify throws OutOfShape; purpose-less requests carry own() only.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T213034Z-ef7ccd2a17aa97dd","text":"Field-format fill candidates carry fieldFormat provenance and conversion assumptions through both verifier wordings; planner validation traces a genuine mint to its original window source and rechecks provenance, since formatted text need not occur verbatim.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T215427Z-85a4a1e31491fed7","text":"Every request slot needs a row in helper/src/privacy/shapes.ts: Disclosure.verify throws OutOfShape for a path with no row, a mint reason the row disallows, or text over its max; a request with no purpose may carry only own() wording.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e5f9cbd94aab9fee","sum":"All app builds run privacy_gate.sh: accepted.ts needs pv2-sites-send + ha2-copied-conversation; Vercel dev opt-in refused; onboarding shows bundled PrivacyPromise.txt; release sets CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1. Disclosure keys match KEY (note_1); dynamic maps need a shapes.ts childGlob.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"009e4aa697218076","sum":"privacy_gate.sh runs on every build (Debug, build-app.sh, helper bundling): accepted.ts records pv2-sites-send and ha2-copied-conversation; CARET_DEV_VERCEL_GEMINI=1 refused; onboarding renders PrivacyPromise.txt; release sets CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1 (no Vercel).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T001204Z-bb38791614f982ff","text":"Caret app builds, including Debug, run scripts/privacy_gate.sh; helper/src/privacy/accepted.ts must record lead acceptance of pv2-sites-send and ha2-copied-conversation before builds pass, and CARET_DEV_VERCEL_GEMINI=1 is refused at build time.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T002947Z-c019705c5089f866","text":"The privacy gate also covers apps/caret/scripts/build-app.sh and direct helper bundling; onboarding must render generated Contents/Resources/PrivacyPromise.txt. Release child environments set CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1, which refuses every Vercel route even with a dev opt-in.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ceaba173a4e941d3","sum":"Xcode privacy phases: first checks source plists, last needs the processed bundle plist. Release env extraction keeps only TypeSafe settings. Disclosure.walk refuses body keys with spaces (use note_1); dynamic state maps need a childGlob rule in shapes.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T004510Z-16ddc03f0a00f357","text":"Xcode's first privacy phase checks source plists; its last requires the processed bundle plist as an input. Release helper env-file extraction preserves TypeSafe key/provider/model/cap and refuses other providers before spawn.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T030901Z-9525a678a3afd6cf","text":"Disclosure.walk refuses any request-body key outside KEY (no spaces), so ids like 'note 1' cannot be state keys (INT1 uses note_1); a state map with dynamic keys also needs a childGlob rule in privacy/shapes.ts besides its .* row.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
